279    /** FUNCTION otap_util.build_msg
280    * Builds a message from a template identifier. Fetches the template and fills the given
281    * variables in p_param1-5 with the given value, if the parameters are filled. Type has
282    * special translation handling for filling the @type@ variable, if it exists in the template and
283    * type label is not NULL. Must be a label from otap_identifiers view like LABEL_COLUMN or LABEL_TABLE.
284    *
285    * Leaving all parameters apart from p_cfg_template empty will return just the current translation of
286    * a config or label value, according to OTAP_TRANSLATE or the default.
287    *
288    * Parameters must contain leading and trailing @ variable indicator. Ignored if not a otap variable
289    * in style @varname@.
290    *
291    * @param p_cfg_template The config name of the template. See otap_util.CFG_ constants.
292    * @param p_type_label The label name of the @type@ variable, if needed. See otap_util.CFG_LABEL constants.
293    * @param p_param1 The 1st variable name in @variable@ notation. If @type@ ignored. Optional.
294    * @param p_param1_value The substitution value for the 1st variable name. Parameter ignored if not given. Optional.
295    * @param p_param2 The 2nd variable name in @variable@ notation. If @type@ ignored. Optional.
296    * @param p_param2_value The substitution value for the 2nd variable name. Parameter ignored if not given. Optional.
297    * @param p_param3 The 3rd variable name in @variable@ notation. If @type@ ignored. Optional.
298    * @param p_param3_value The substitution value for the 3rd variable name. Parameter ignored if not given. Optional.
299    * @param p_param4 The 4th variable name in @variable@ notation. If @type@ ignored. Optional.
300    * @param p_param4_value The substitution value for the 4th variable name. Parameter ignored if not given. Optional.
301    * @param p_param5 The 5th variable name in @variable@ notation. If @type@ ignored. Optional.
302    * @param p_param5_value The substitution value for the 5th variable name. Parameter ignored if not given. Optional.
303    * @param p_description A template overwrite. Will return the given description instead of the template. Optional.
304    *
305    * @return The message build from template, overwritten by description or an error message.
306    */
307    FUNCTION build_msg( p_cfg_template  IN VARCHAR2
308  			 , p_type_label    IN VARCHAR2 DEFAULT NULL
309  			 , p_param1	   IN VARCHAR2 DEFAULT NULL
310  			 , p_param1_value  IN VARCHAR2 DEFAULT NULL
311  			 , p_param2	   IN VARCHAR2 DEFAULT NULL
312  			 , p_param2_value  IN VARCHAR2 DEFAULT NULL
313  			 , p_param3	   IN VARCHAR2 DEFAULT NULL
