151    /** FUNCTION otap_generate.schema_tests
152    * Generates the test scripts for the current available otap schema functions.
153    * Provides set, group and name management.  Limited to line size 4000 but not to rows,
154    * like DBMS_OUTPUT. It is up to you how you spool the content to files.
155    *
156    * Including system generated objects is a good idea if your system is stable and you want to
157    * ensure that no one changed the current state. With CI/CD or during development it is a really bad idea.
158    *
159    * There is no best option, some constraints like NOT NULL must be defined inline to count a column as NOT NULL.
160    * With an additional added constraint, the column will be still marked as NULLABLE. Identity columns are another
161    * issue, as you cannot define a name for the generated sequence. Make extra tests limited on the system generated
162    * objects you rely on (like NOT NULL and identity).
163    *
164    * @param p_schema The schema to generate the tests for. Default is current schema.
165    * @param p_title_prefix An optional title prefix for set, group and test names. Limited to 10 chars.
166    * @param p_show_header Used to surpress header comments, init, count and finish section. Default 1 will contain all sections, otherwise skipped.
167    * @param p_excl_sysgen Used to ignore system generated objects identified by SYS_ or $. Default 1 will ignore system generated objects, otherwise included.
168    *
169    * @return An OTAP_VIEW_RESULT_REC object as table type OTAP_VIEW_RESULT_TBL.
170    */
